<title>HUNGARY: Inter-Europa Q1 pre-tax profit rises yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Inter-Europa Q1 pre-tax profit rises yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three-month period ending on March 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>						   Q1 1997	   Q1 1996</p>
<p>    Operating profit			   641.0    vs     605.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			     651.1    vs     613.4</p>
<p>    Interest received			4,582.7    vs   3,456.1</p>
<p>    Interest paid			    3,792.9    vs   2,688.2</p>
<p>    Net interest income			789.8    vs     768.0</p>
<p>    Dividend received			    2.4    vs	 2.0</p>
<p>    Other operating revenue		  722.6    vs     486.5</p>
<p>    Other revenue				 14.5    vs	 6.8</p>
<p>    Other operating expenditure	    174.2    vs     105.8</p>
<p>    Other expenditure			   74.6    vs	65.1</p>
<p>    Risk reserves created		     36.4    vs	 0</p>
<p>    Operating costs			    639.5    vs     486.9</p>
<p>    Non-operating revenue (leasing)	  9.6    vs	 8.9</p>
<p>    Non-operating expend. (leasing)	  9.6    vs	 8.9</p>
<p>    Extraordinari profit			10.1    vs	 7.9</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total (March 31)    95,110.3    vs  64,930.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is Inter-Europa Bank Rt. The figures are unconsolidated, unaudited and were calculated according to the Hungarian accounting standard. Italy's Istituto Bancario San Paolo di Torino holds a controlling stake in Inter-Europa.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
